      "writtenOn": "2020-02-13T11:28:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As far as I understood schedtune behavior was the spec here and this matches what we\u0027ve done before.\n\nIIUC, Android will set a blanket value 50ms for all tasks.\n\nOne of the things I requested more feedback on from the google team is how much necessary this functionality is to push for a generic upstream solution. I want to see the real world use-case from google to implement the more complex solution. Otherwise it seems a waste of effort? Conor tested uclamp vs schedtune without this functionality and the numbers seemed fine. So maybe we no longer need this feature on recent kernels given the improvements in other areas?\n\nDo you see an easy implementation option here that we missed without having to keep track of the state (expiration, min_value) for every enqueued task on the rq? If you do, then I\u0027ll be happy to just do it :)",
