    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9a8ae63b_59694021",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/core.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1004,
      "author": {
        "id": 1456182
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-02-13T11:28:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Chris was using the rq-\u003euclamp[UCLAMP_MIN].value but I changed it to uclamp_eff_value().\n\nMy concern was that in the rq you can have a task with high uclamp.min value but it doesn\u0027t request any hold.\n\nSo if we have:\n\n     1. task_a-\u003euclamp.min \u003d 800 \u0026\u0026 task_a-\u003ehold_ms \u003d 0\n     2. task_b-\u003euclamp.min \u003d 400 \u0026\u0026 task_b-\u003ehold_ms \u003d 50\n     3. enqueue(task_a)\n     4. enqueue(task_b)\n\nIf we use rq-\u003euclamp[UCLAMP_MIN].value it\u0027d be 800. But since task_a has no hold then we shouldn\u0027t use this value as the min hold but task_b\u0027s value of 400.\n\nMakes sense or did I miss something?",
      "parentUuid": "8f880c4c_cf3a5796",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1001,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 1004,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "57f5222d45202ddba531159535ed6e98b1c0e11c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
